### Intelligent Customer Support System — sample requests
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into curl/Postman.
@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health check
GET {{base}}/

### 1. Create a ticket (201)
POST {{base}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-1001",
  "customer_email": "olena@example.com",
  "customer_name": "Olena Shevchenko",
  "subject": "Cannot log in after password reset",
  "description": "I reset my password but now I am locked out of my account. This is critical for my work.",
  "tags": ["login", "urgent-review"],
  "metadata": { "source": "web_form", "browser": "Chrome 126", "device_type": "desktop" }
}

### 2. Create with auto-classification (note category/priority get filled)
POST {{base}}/tickets?autoClassify=true
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-1002",
  "customer_email": "dmytro@example.com",
  "subject": "Production down — login page error 500",
  "description": "The login page shows error 500 for all users. This is urgent and blocking the whole team."
}

### 3. Validation error (400) — bad email, short description
POST {{base}}/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "CUST-1003",
  "customer_email": "not-an-email",
  "subject": "Broken request",
  "description": "too short"
}

### 4. Bulk import — CSV (50 tickets, with auto-classification)
POST {{base}}/tickets/import?format=csv&autoClassify=true
Content-Type: text/csv

< ../tests/fixtures/sample_tickets.csv

### 5. Bulk import — JSON (20 tickets)
POST {{base}}/tickets/import
Content-Type: application/json

< ../tests/fixtures/sample_tickets.json

### 6. Bulk import — XML (30 tickets)
POST {{base}}/tickets/import
Content-Type: application/xml

< ../tests/fixtures/sample_tickets.xml

### 7. Bulk import — invalid records (per-record error report)
POST {{base}}/tickets/import?format=json
Content-Type: application/json

< ../tests/fixtures/invalid_tickets.json

### 8. List all tickets
GET {{base}}/tickets

### 9. Combined filtering: category + priority
GET {{base}}/tickets?category=account_access&priority=urgent

### 10. Filter by status + full-text search
GET {{base}}/tickets?status=new&q=refund

### 11. Get one ticket (replace the id)
GET {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID

### 12. Auto-classify an existing ticket
POST {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID/auto-classify

### 13. Auto-classify dry-run (report only, no changes)
POST {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID/auto-classify?apply=false

### 14. Manual override (logged as manual_override in the audit trail)
PUT {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{ "category": "billing_question", "priority": "high" }

### 15. Classification audit log for a ticket
GET {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID/classification-log

### 16. Resolve a ticket (sets resolved_at)
PUT {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "resolved" }

### 17. Delete a ticket (204)
DELETE {{base}}/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_ID
